WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.449 --> 00:00:06.109
Speaker 1: But as I mentioned, if you want
to lay the blame for the failures in Afghanistan

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:11.720
at anybody's feet, it has to be at the feet
of George W. Bush.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:18.190
And right now, both Biden and twice impeached
former President Donald Trump seem to want

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.830
to lay the blame at each other's feet.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.500
You've got members of the Biden administration
coming out and saying no to everything that's

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.760
happening right now is Donald Trump's fault.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.090
And then Trump, of course, is issuing his
idiotic statement saying, look at all these

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.750
failures of Biden, I left him a road map and
he didn't follow it.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.980
This is his fault.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:45.420
These two going back and forth and back and
forth, completely ignoring.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.150
This all started under George W. Bush, folks,
and I know I've said this plenty of times

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.180
have already said it today.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.630
It's going through four administrations at
this point.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.540
But.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:01.730
George W. Bush's name was not mentioned once
on the Sunday talk shows this past week and

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.070
now once.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:11.009
You cannot talk about Afghanistan without
talking about George W. Bush and the failures

00:01:11.009 --> 00:01:19.049
of the war on terror, the failures of this
nation building that we went on over there.

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:25.880
That's where all the failures began and yes,
it is accurate to say that both Democrat and

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:32.799
Republican administrations came along after
that and continued this disastrous policy.

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:37.500
But they weren't the ones who implemented
it, everyone who has inherited this Afghanistan

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.020
mess since George W. Bush left office hasn't
had a roadmap.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:46.630
They haven't known what the heck to do over
there.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.359
So we keep bombing, we keep sending weapons.

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:54.689
We keep the killing going, we keep the troops
over there, maybe we're going to bring a home

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:58.740
that maybe we're not, you know, that happened
during Obama and then instead.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.729
Oh, no, we're going to send more.

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:03.229
Happened under we're going to bring him home.

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:05.249
No way we got it, we got we got to send a
few more.

00:02:05.249 --> 00:02:08.200
We're going to put more military contractors
over there were going to bring troops back,

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.200
some of them.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.549
But we're going to double down on the number
of military contractors we have over there.

00:02:13.549 --> 00:02:17.460
That also happen, by the way, earlier this
year with the Biden administration, because

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.470
nobody has known.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:22.630
What to do?

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:26.770
Because there was never any real goal.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:34.170
The so-called war on terror was such a vague
concept that it could mean anything, and we

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:41.260
went into it obviously with a lot of hostility
following 9/11, we were not thinking clearly

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.599
as a nation.

00:02:42.599 --> 00:02:43.659
We wanted revenge.

00:02:43.659 --> 00:02:44.659
We wanted retribution.

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:51.069
And, of course, because George W. Bush had
all these, you know, former officials from

00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:55.900
the first Gulf War in his administration,
they wanted to go back over there and finish

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.989
the job.

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:01.870
So they focused on Iraq, they kept Afghanistan
over there on the back burner.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.079
We had to do Taliban.

00:03:03.079 --> 00:03:04.079
Yeah, we're going to get them.

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:06.680
But Iraq was the big prize.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.010
So Afghanistan fell by the wayside.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.010
We still kept troops there.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.150
We still kept fighting there.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:16.481
But never really had a plan there that was
kind of just the for show part, oh, we're

00:03:16.481 --> 00:03:20.069
looking for bin Laden over in Afghanistan,
that's that's what we're doing over there.

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:21.460
But, hey, we just got Saddam Hussein.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.460
Right.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.560
And that's that's what everybody wanted.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.939
Following 9/11, as Corey Robin pointed out
on Twitter the other day.

00:03:29.939 --> 00:03:35.659
Ninety percent of the American public supported
sending troops to Afghanistan.

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:39.629
So when I say we weren't thinking clearly
as a nation, that's the kind of thing I'm

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:44.950
talking about here, 90 percent of people supported
this thing, not knowing what it was really

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.690
about, not knowing what was going on.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:54.569
But George Bush and his administration lied
us over there and got us stuck.

00:03:54.569 --> 00:03:59.700
And then they left and Obama continued, then
he left and Trump continued.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:05.310
Now we've got Biden pulling troops out, Trump
saying, Oh, look at what an idiot you are.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:09.799
Again, ignoring the fact that just a few months
ago, he was begging Biden to finish what he

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:14.560
started pulling all the troops out.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:19.910
At this point, it wouldn't have mattered if
we had pulled troops out of there in 24 or

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:26.750
20, 10 or 20, 20 or even 20, 30, this would
have happened.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.380
This same thing that we're watching unfold
right now with the Taliban capturing Kabul,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.810
this still would have happened.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:41.760
Because there was no goal, there was no strategy,
there was no actual peace deal negotiated

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:48.190
between the U.S. government and the Taliban
and the Afghani government, and this is what

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.290
we got.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:54.790
This is the disaster that we have to deal
with now.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:58.660
And again, I don't think anybody really knows
what to do about this.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:03.480
Do we just let the Taliban take over, walk
away and say, well, good luck, you got a mess

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.820
on your hands?

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:09.450
I don't agree with sending troops back over
there, I think it's just another disaster,

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.820
you're just prolonging this from happening
again.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:19.810
And nobody knows the answer, the answer, though,
is that we have to continue to help the people

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.910
of Afghanistan.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:26.230
We need to be able to get them out of the
country, we need to take in as many refugees

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:28.850
as we possibly can here in the United States.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:32.100
I don't want to hear anger from conservatives
about this.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.970
We put them in this situation.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.690
We've got to take care of them.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.050
And that's the best thing we can do right
now.

